-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Building ATHENA
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA is built with CMake. The inherited GNU autotools files are not maintained
for ATHENA.

The supported and tested development path is Linux. The tree still contains
inherited Windows and macOS branches, but the ATHENA build process has not been
tested on Windows or macOS.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dependencies
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA intentionally assumes a modern desktop development environment. The
CMake configuration currently requires, among others:

  CMake, a C/C++ compiler, pkg-config, Qt 6, Guile 1.8, mimalloc, SQLite3,
  Python 3, uv, FreeType, PNG, JPEG, zlib, zstd, ImageMagick/MagickWand,
  Iconv, GnuTLS, GMP, Ghostscript, resvg with ResvgQt.h, libtcc, and patchelf.

On openSUSE, this is a useful zypper baseline for the ordinary system
dependencies:

  sudo zypper install \
    git cmake ninja pkgconf-pkg-config patchelf \
    qt6-base-devel qt6-svg-devel qt6-wayland-devel qt6-qt5compat-devel \
    kf6-kio-devel kf6-kconfigwidgets-devel \
    mimalloc-devel sqlite3-devel \
    python3 python313-uv \
    freetype2-devel libpng16-devel libjpeg8-devel zlib-devel \
    libzstd-devel ImageMagick-devel \
    libgnutls-devel gmp-devel ghostscript resvg-devel

Package names vary by distribution and repository. If CMake reports that
ResvgQt.h or libtcc is missing, install the corresponding development package
from your distribution or a local package/source build. ATHENA uses libtcc for
namespace sorter support.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Guile 1.8
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA currently needs Guile 1.8. Do not rely on a modern distribution's default
Guile development package unless it actually provides Guile 1.8 pkg-config
metadata.

The Guile 1.8 package used for the verified build is:

  https://build.opensuse.org/package/show/home:jmnotin:TeXmacs/Guile18

Build and install Guile 1.8 separately before configuring ATHENA. If the package
is installed system-wide and pkg-config can already find guile-1.8, no extra
environment variable is needed. If you install it under a private prefix, for
example $HOME/opt/guile18, export its pkg-config path before running CMake:

  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$HOME/opt/guile18/lib64/pkgconfig:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH"

Verify that pkg-config sees the correct version:

  pkg-config --modversion guile-1.8

The verified build used Guile 1.8.8.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DataArt Python environment
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA's DataArt PDF cover generator is a uv-managed Python project in
ATHENA/tools/data-art. CMake synchronizes its locked Python environment during
the build by running:

  uv sync --locked --no-dev --project ATHENA/tools/data-art

The generated ATHENA/tools/data-art/.venv directory is build/runtime state. Do
not commit it to source control. For a binary archive, either include a deliberate
offline runtime bundle or require the packager to run the CMake build once so uv
can synchronize the environment.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recommended compiler: Intel oneAPI ICPX
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ATHENA strongly recommends Intel oneAPI C++ (icpx). The project is large, and
icpx has been the preferred compiler during current ATHENA development.

Example oneAPI setup on an RPM/zypper based system:

  sudo rpm --import \
    https://yum.repos.intel.com/oneapi/GPG-PUB-KEY-INTEL-SW-PRODUCTS.PUB
  sudo zypper addrepo -f https://yum.repos.intel.com/oneapi oneAPI
  sudo zypper refresh
  sudo zypper install intel-oneapi-compiler-dpcpp-cpp

Before configuring ATHENA, load the oneAPI environment:

  source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh
  which icx
  which icpx

If the build directory was previously configured with another compiler, remove
it before switching compilers.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Configure and build
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

From the repository root:

  source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$HOME/opt/guile18/lib64/pkgconfig:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH"

  CC=icx CXX=icpx cmake -S . -B build_qt6 \
    -DATHENA_GUI=Qt6 \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug

  CCACHE_DISABLE=1 cmake --build build_qt6 -j "$(nproc)"

Using all available processor cores is recommended; `nproc` is the preferred
way to pick the parallelism level.

Pass `-G Ninja` if you prefer Ninja; the currently used local Qt6 build
directory was configured with CMake's default Unix Makefiles generator.

CMake patches the built executable with:

  RUNPATH=$ORIGIN/../lib

This lets a copied ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin resolve bundled libraries from
ATHENA/lib without manually running patchelf.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Run from the source runtime tree
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For ATHENA development, do not run the executable directly from build_qt6/src.
Copy the build output into the ATHENA runtime tree first:

  cp -f build_qt6/src/ATHENA.bin ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin
  mkdir -p ATHENA/lib
  cp -a build_qt6/x64/lib/libqt6advanceddockingd.so* ATHENA/lib/

Then run:

  ./ATHENA/StartATHENA.sh

This matters because ATHENA expects its Scheme code, packages, tools, assets,
and runtime paths to be arranged under the ATHENA tree.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Assemble a binary release tree
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

To prepare the runtime directory that will later be packaged:

  rm -rf release/ATHENA
  mkdir -p release
  rsync -a ATHENA/ release/ATHENA/

  install -m 755 build_qt6/src/ATHENA.bin release/ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin
  mkdir -p release/ATHENA/lib
  rm -f release/ATHENA/lib/libqt*advanceddocking*.so*
  cp -a build_qt6/x64/lib/libqt6advanceddockingd.so* release/ATHENA/lib/

Useful checks:

  readelf -d release/ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin | \
    grep -E 'RUNPATH|RPATH|qt6advanced'
  readelf -d release/ATHENA/lib/libqt6advanceddockingd.so.4.3.1 | \
    grep -E 'RUNPATH|RPATH|SONAME'
  ldd release/ATHENA/bin/ATHENA.bin | grep qt6advanceddocking

The ADS library should resolve from release/ATHENA/lib. The executable should
have RUNPATH $ORIGIN/../lib. The ADS library itself should not carry an
absolute build rpath.

Run the release tree with:

  ./release/ATHENA/StartATHENA.sh

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Install
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For a system install, use the usual CMake install workflow:

  cmake --install build_qt6

Set a custom prefix at configure time if needed:

  source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$HOME/opt/guile18/lib64/pkgconfig:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH"
  CC=icx CXX=icpx cmake -S . -B build_qt6 \
    -DATHENA_GUI=Qt6 \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
    -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/athena

The primary tested workflow is the ATHENA runtime tree described above; use
CMake install only if you intentionally want a system-style installation.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Troubleshooting
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

If CMake cannot find a dependency, install the corresponding development package
and rerun the configure step. If CMake cannot find Guile 1.8 specifically, check
PKG_CONFIG_PATH and verify:

  pkg-config --modversion guile-1.8

If generated files or Scheme cache entries interfere with a local development
build, remove the build directory and ATHENA cache, then configure again:

  rm -rf build_qt6
  rm -rf ~/.ATHENA/system/cache
  source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH="$HOME/opt/guile18/lib64/pkgconfig:$PKG_CONFIG_PATH"
  CC=icx CXX=icpx cmake -S . -B build_qt6 \
    -DATHENA_GUI=Qt6 \
    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
